course: dictionary
lesson: 13308
title: Gremlins in the works
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gremlin is an imaginary, mischievous little creature. People blame gremlins when machines go wrong, even though gremlins are not real. The word is also used informally for a small, unknown fault that makes a machine stop working. «Our tablet keeps switching off, so there must be a gremlin in it.»
explain: Use the context to find the meaning. The tablet keeps switching off for no clear reason, and nobody can see what is wrong. So a gremlin here means a hidden fault, not a creature. Check by swapping in your meaning: «there must be a hidden fault in it» still makes sense.
explain: Writers often use gremlins as a joke. «Dad joked that gremlins had stolen the TV remote.» Dad does not really believe it, because gremlins are imaginary. The joke shows that something has gone wrong and nobody knows why.
explain: Look out for phrases with gremlin in them. «A gremlin in the works» means a hidden problem stopping a machine working properly. «Technical gremlins» means small faults in machines or computers. Phrases like these have their own meanings, so think about the whole phrase, not just one word.
fact: A gremlin is an imaginary, mischievous little creature blamed for things going wrong with machines.
fact: In everyday talk, «gremlin» can mean a small, unknown fault that makes a machine or computer break down.
fact: The idea started with pilots in the Royal Air Force in the 1920s to 1940s, who blamed plane faults on gremlins.
fact: Gremlins are famous from stories and films, such as «Gremlins», where they are naughty creatures.
fact: «A gremlin in the works» means a hidden problem stopping something working properly.
exercise: «Our tablet keeps switching off for no reason. Dad says there must be a gremlin in it.» What does gremlin mean here? | A new game app | A small pet that lives inside the tablet | *An unknown small fault that makes a machine break down | A kind helper who fixes the tablet
exercise: Lily says, «Gremlins stole my homework!» Why is she probably joking? | Gremlins are real animals that live in schools | Gremlins are a kind of homework | *Gremlins are imaginary, so they could not really steal anything | Gremlins always tell the truth about homework
exercise: «The mischievous gremlin pulled the plug out of the wall.» Find and copy one word that means playfully naughty. | wall | pulled | plug | *mischievous
test: «The pilots blamed gremlins for the faults in their planes.» Where did the idea of blaming gremlins for machine faults start? | With Victorian children in their schools | With farmers in the 1800s | In a film made in the 1990s | *With pilots in the Royal Air Force, in the 1920s to 1940s
test: «The lights flickered all evening, so Mum said there was a gremlin in the wiring.» What does a gremlin in the wiring suggest? | A creature that lives in the lights | *A hidden fault causing the problem | A power cut that lasts all week | A new kind of light bulb
exam: «The printer has technical gremlins again.» What is the best meaning of technical gremlins? | Very large printers that are hard to move | Bad weather that stops the Wi-Fi | Friendly robots that help the teachers at school | *Small, hidden faults that keep machines from working properly
